title: Cafe_Enter
---
<<if met("flag:cafe_entered")>>
The bell rings. The door swings shut behind you again, and the frost seals it.
<<else>>
The bell over the door rings as you step inside.
<<if met("flag:clue_underpass_bells")>>
The same bells you heard from the underpass.
<<endif>>
The lamps are lit, but the room is as cold as the street. Cups sit frozen to their saucers.
Behind you, the door swings shut. Frost runs across the glass and seals it.
<<flag cafe_entered>>
<<endif>>
===
title: Cafe_GiveIn
---
The door won't open. The cold is in your fingers now.
You could sit down for a moment. Just close your eyes.
-> Stay awake.
    You shake your head. Not yet.
-> Sit down and close your eyes.
    You sink into the armchair by the cold stove. Snow keeps falling past the window.
    <<wake_up "You fell asleep in the cold.">>
===
title: Cafe_MenuBoard
---
Chalk on the board. SUMIYAKI COFFEE, roasted over charcoal, here, every morning. 350 yen.
===
title: Cafe_Siphon
---
A coffee siphon, half full. The coffee has frozen into brown glass. Someone was in the middle of making it.
===
title: Cafe_Register
---
The till drawer hangs open, empty. A sticker on the side says KISSA MORI, SINCE 1971.
===
title: Cafe_Charcoal
---
<<if met("item:charcoal | item:kindling | flag:cafe_stove_loaded")>>
The sack of roasting charcoal. You already have what you need from it.
<<else>>
A sack of charcoal for the roaster. You take a handful.
<<give charcoal>>
<<endif>>
===
title: Cafe_Plate
---
A brass plate under the three dials, engraved in plain letters.
SPEAK THE OLD RULE, AND I WILL BURN.
<<if met("flag:tablet_read")>>
The old rule. The tablet in the shrine hall had one, and you remember it, top to bottom.
GATE, two posts and a beam. COLD, three strokes, each shorter than the last. SLEEP, a closed eye. FIRE, three flames, the middle one tallest. WAKE, an open eye in a frame.
"Through the gate, into the cold, one sleeps. Only a fire wakes the sleeper."
<<endif>>
<<flag clue_cafe_lock>>
===
title: Cafe_StoveLocked
---
The firebox door won't budge. The three dials above it hold it shut.
===
title: Cafe_LockOpens
---
The last dial clicks into place. Inside the stove, a bolt slides back, and the firebox door swings open.
===
title: Cafe_DialsBlind
---
Signs cut into brass. You can't read them, and turning them blind does nothing.
===
title: Cafe_DialsSet
---
The dials won't turn any more. The lock is open.
===
title: Cafe_StoveEmpty
---
The firebox is open. Cold ash, and nothing to burn.
===
title: Cafe_CharcoalAlone
---
Charcoal won't catch from a match on its own. It needs something that burns fast first.
===
title: Cafe_PaperAlone
---
Paper on its own would flare up and die. It needs something to keep it going.
===
title: Cafe_NothingToBurn
---
There's nothing in the firebox to light.
===
title: Cafe_Loaded
---
You pack the kindling into the firebox.
===
title: Cafe_StoveReady
---
Kindling waits in the firebox. It only needs a flame.
===
title: Cafe_Fire
---
The match catches the paper, and the paper catches the charcoal.
The stove ticks, then roars. For the first time, warmth spills into the room.
The frost on the windows starts to run.
Only a fire wakes the sleeper.
===
title: Cafe_Armchair
---
A worn armchair, turned toward the stove. Sitting down would be very easy.
===
title: Cafe_Door
---
The door has frozen shut behind you. Ice fills the frame. You won't get out this way.
===
title: Cafe_Bell
---
A brass bell over the door.
<<if met("flag:clue_underpass_bells")>>
The bells you heard from the underpass. Small ones, the kind that hang on a shop door.
<<endif>>
===
title: Cafe_Window
---
Snow falls past the glass. The street outside is already gone under it.
===
title: Cafe_Newspaper
---
<<if met("item:newspaper | item:kindling | flag:cafe_stove_loaded")>>
Only the ads are left on the table.
<<else>>
A newspaper on the table, dry and folded. The date has been torn off. You take it.
<<give newspaper>>
<<endif>>
===
title: Cafe_Photo
---
A photo of an old man by this stove, laughing, a match in his hand.
Under it, in pen, someone has written "Mori's stove only listens to the old rule."
<<flag clue_cafe_stove>>
===
title: Made_kindling
---
You twist the newspaper around a handful of charcoal. Kindling.
===
